{"name":"Crumbly Lipstick","hex":"#ee66bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crumbly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easy to break into small fragments; brittle or friable."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A decrepit old person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crumbly"},{"term":"lipstick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Makeup for the lips.","A stick of this makeup."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply lipstick to; to paint with lipstick."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lipstick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lipstick","blocks":[{"text":"Lipstick is a cosmetic product used to apply color and texture to lips, often made of wax and oil. Different pigments are used to produce color, and minerals such as silica may be used to provide texture. The use of lipstick dates back to early civilizations such as Sumer and the Indus Valley Civilisation, and was popularized in the Western world in the 16th century. Some lipsticks contain traces of toxic materials, such as lead and PFAS, which prompted health concerns and regulation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Applying_red_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg/330px-Applying_red_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lipstick"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Magenta_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg/500px-Magenta_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Magenta_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg/1280px-Magenta_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Magenta_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg/500px-Magenta_lipstick_-_mod